1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:21,001
One park, one shared picture
Actual OVRTX rendering; all source data, scenarios and operational actions are synthetic.

2
00:00:21,001 --> 00:00:27,234
Explore the connected park
Orbit, zoom and click scene geometry to resolve its asset identity and connected data.

3
00:00:27,234 --> 00:00:45,006
Selection follows the rendered scene
A changing view causes retries here; selection succeeds against the current scene.

4
00:00:45,006 --> 00:01:17,001
Compare, respond and trace
Compare a modeled ride closure, apply it, dispatch maintenance and inspect the audit trail.

5
00:01:17,001 --> 00:01:47,001
Understand utility dependencies
Trace logical power dependencies, shed flexible load and simulate a water-leak repair.

6
00:01:47,001 --> 00:02:11,611
Coordinate guests and wellbeing
Respond to show-departure demand and heatwave scenarios with rerouting and qualified staff.

7
00:02:11,611 --> 00:02:27,001
Connect inventory to operations
A food-rush scenario connects queues, staffing and ERP inventory to a replenishment action.

8
00:02:27,001 --> 00:03:02,541
Inspect sources and their quality
Explore the API architecture, then pause a source and watch accepted observations become stale.

9
00:03:02,541 --> 00:03:16,181
Replay a recorded moment
Review recorded state in a shared read-only view; camera navigation remains interactive.

10
00:03:16,181 --> 00:03:27,004
Return to live operations
One asset backbone connects operations, source provenance, recorded history and the real rendered scene.
